# LF for the check scripts. They are copied verbatim into the generated Copilot build, so the source
# and its copy must stay byte-identical. Without this rule a checkout under core.autocrlf=true
# restores CRLF while the build emits LF, and the two diverge.
# Written as a property of that SETTING, never of one machine: an earlier version of this comment
# asserted "this machine runs core.autocrlf=true" and went stale the day the global config changed.
# The matching `github_build/** text eol=lf` rule is gone: the build is no longer committed
# (docs/adr/0003), so git never stores or restores those files.
scripts/*.mjs text eol=lf
